CHAPTER.VERS:
Ho Ariel, Ariel, the city where David encamped! Add

          {+}
         year to year; let the feasts come round:

Tarry

          {+}
         and wonder; take your

          {+}
         pleasure and be blind: they are drunk, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink.

For Yahweh has poured out on you

          {+}
         the spirit of deep sleep, and has closed your

          {+}
         eyes, the prophets; and your

          {+}
         heads, the seers, he has covered.

And all vision has become to you

          {+}
         as the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one who is learned, saying, Read this, I pray you; and he says, I can't, for it is sealed:

You

          {+}
         turn things upside down! Will the potter be esteemed as clay; that the thing made should say of him who made it, He didn't make me; or the thing formed say of him who formed it, He has no understanding?
